      "name": null,
      "problem": "Factor $\\frac{8}{{t}^{6}}-1000.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}-{b}^{3}=(a-b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that all of the terms have a common factor of $8.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $8,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{{t}^{6}}-1000=8(\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}}-125)\n$$\n\nThe expression in parentheses can be written as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\n8(\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}}-125)=8({(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{3}-{5}^{3})\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression in parentheses using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{t}^{6}}-1000 & =8({(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{3}-{5}^{3}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-5)({(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 5+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-5)(\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}+25)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
